IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sk73-nouns`
IMPORT `sk73-cross-references`

-- Row il-73. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the two items: the status of each enactment, the dates of the issues as their footers print them, the commencement values and how each was obtained, both limbs and how each was read, the series flag, and the tag table.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The two assertions that the references do NOT hold are in sk73-tests-red.l4.
-- The expected values are hand-written from NOTES.md (the answer tables), not copied from the references module.

§ `Tests of the readings for item I1`

#ASSERT `the Bankruptcy Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`'s `its status` EQUALS `repealed but for one section`
#ASSERT `the Companies Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`'s `its status` EQUALS `repealed in part`
#ASSERT `the enactment is repealed in whole or in part` `the Bankruptcy Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`
#ASSERT `the enactment is repealed in whole or in part` `the Companies Ordinance as section 4A(b)(2) names it`
#ASSERT `some enactment the citing words name is repealed in whole or in part` `item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`
#ASSERT NOT (`no enactment the citing words name is repealed in whole or in part` `item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`)
#ASSERT `both limbs hold for the enactments` `item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`
#ASSERT NOT (`item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`'s `a later instruction changes a name the citing words print`)
#ASSERT `item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page images of the instruments named`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 4A(b)(2) names two enactments`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page images, with the other instruments of the consolidation's tag table read and later instruments not excluded (see NOTES.md)`

-- Pair (11) is the pair of the 2014 law that reaches (b)(2), and it replaces the word with its prefix and the word for employer by the word for employer in the new term.
#ASSERT `pair (11) of SH 2459 section 1`'s `the number of the pair` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `pair (11) of SH 2459 section 1`'s `the word replaced` EQUALS "שהמעביד"
#ASSERT `pair (11) of SH 2459 section 1`'s `the word put in its place` EQUALS "שהמעסיק"
#ASSERT `the pairs of SH 2459 section 1 searched for the two names`'s `the number of pairs` EQUALS 84

-- The dates are the dates the footers print (issue dates), not days of effect.
#ASSERT `issue SH 2203`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 23 7 2009)
#ASSERT `issue SH 2459`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2014)
#ASSERT `issue SH 2708`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2018)

-- The commencement of SH 2708: printed as 18 months from publication; 15.9.2019 is a computation from the footer date, not a printed date, and the footer date is not the commencement.
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2708 as printed`'s `the rule as printed, in English` EQUALS "18 months from its publication"
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2708 as printed`'s `the day it names` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 9 2019)
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2708 as printed`'s `how the day was obtained` EQUALS `computed from the issue date, not printed`
#ASSERT NOT (`the commencement of SH 2708 as printed`'s `the day it names` EQUALS `issue SH 2708`'s `the date its footer prints`)

-- SH 2203 section 132: no commencement section was read, so there is no day.
#ASSERT `the day the instruction takes effect` `SH 2203 section 132` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2203 section 132, not read`'s `the day it names` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2203 section 132, not read`'s `how the day was obtained` EQUALS `not given by any page read`

-- The series flag of the 1983 print: a new-version print whose footers print no date.
#ASSERT `issue DMI 37`'s `its series` EQUALS `Dinei Medinat Israel new-version print, not one of the three gazette series`
#ASSERT `issue DMI 37`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `issue SH 2708`'s `its series` EQUALS `Sefer HaChukim`

§ `Tests of the readings for item I2`

#ASSERT `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`'s `the number the citing words write for the chapter` EQUALS "ג׳2"
#ASSERT `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`'s `the number in the heading of the later print` EQUALS "ו׳"
#ASSERT `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`'s `the table row of the later print, 1968 entry` EQUALS "ג׳2"
#ASSERT `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`'s `the table row of the later print, 1995 entry` EQUALS "ו׳"
#ASSERT `the number the 1995 print's table gives the cited chapter` `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law` EQUALS JUST "ו׳"
#ASSERT NOT (`item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`'s `the 1995 column of the table holds an entry equal to the number the citing words write`)
#ASSERT `both limbs hold for the chapter` `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 11 cites chapter ג׳2 of the National Insurance Law`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page images of the instruments named`

-- The commencement of SH 856 section 10, by arithmetic on the page's own section 11(b); the footer date is not the commencement.
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 856 section 10`'s `the day it names` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 10 1978)
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 856 section 10`'s `how the day was obtained` EQUALS `arithmetic on words printed on a deposited page`
#ASSERT `issue SH 856`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 25 3 1977)
#ASSERT NOT (`the commencement of SH 856 section 10`'s `the day it names` EQUALS `issue SH 856`'s `the date its footer prints`)
#ASSERT `issue SH 1522`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 5 1995)
#ASSERT `issue SH 814`'s `the date its footer prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 24 6 1976)

§ `Tests of the readings for the tag table`

-- The instruments whose pages carry an instruction on section 4A, and on section 11; every other row carries none.
#ASSERT map `the name of the issue of the row` (filter `the row carries an instruction on section 4A` `the tag-table rows`) EQUALS LIST "SH 2203", "SH 2459"
#ASSERT map `the name of the issue of the row` (filter `the row carries an instruction on section 11` `the tag-table rows`) EQUALS LIST "SH 856"

-- The words of the Interpretation Law as printed are typed and are not compared with anything: the tokens are the printed words of sections 1 and 25.
#ASSERT `SH 1030 section 25 as printed`'s `the printed page` EQUALS 305
#ASSERT `SH 1030 section 1 as printed`'s `the printed page` EQUALS 302
